(1) does SCORE (the commutative a+b face) determine the iso class?
    n=3: #iso=2, #score=2, BIJECTIVE=True
    n=4: #iso=4, #score=4, BIJECTIVE=True
    n=5: #iso=12, #score=9, BIJECTIVE=False  <- score insufficient; the ORDER (a^b/b^a) face is needed

(2) the cap DIP vs |P|=13-k (the compression boundary is |P|=4->5):
    k=8: |P|=5  dip=1081/76440=0.01414  (LARGE, |P|=5 = the n=5 transition = binding)
    k=9: |P|=4  dip=1/4004=0.00025  (tiny, |P|=4 edge)
    k=10: |P|=3  dip=0=0.00000  (=0, compression works |P|<=3)
    k=11: |P|=2  dip=0=0.00000  (=0, compression works |P|<=3)
    k=12: |P|=1  dip=0=0.00000  (=0, compression works |P|<=3)
    k=13: |P|=0  dip=0=0.00000  (=0, compression works |P|<=3)

(3) PARITY split of the gK8 dip term for consec_8 (L_yK8 = 10S0-10S1+10S2 -9S3 +6S4):
    ODD  -9 S3 = -12.135  (antisymmetric / a^b,b^a / orientation / Worpitzky -- codex HYP-3147)
    EVEN +6 S4 = +3.853  (symmetric / a+b,a*b / biquadratic resolvent -- mac-mini S70)
    |odd|/|even| = 3.15  (the ODD/Worpitzky face dominates the k=8 correction)
    n=3 edge-kernel eigenvalue -1/3; Worpitzky A(3,k)=[1,4,1]; x^3=C(x+2,3)+4C(x+1,3)+C(x,3).

=> the k=8 dip = EVEN(biquadratic, solvable degree-2, S70) + ODD(Worpitzky n=3-oscillation, codex);
   it appears EXACTLY at |P|=5 = the n=5 transition where score->iso compression FAILS.
